* ANALYTIC CONTROL for the extraction chain (issue #35) -- NOT a candidate.
*
* An ideal behavioural "mixer" whose every extracted quantity has a closed
* form, run through exactly the same ports (ports_common.spice), deck
* generator, in-deck DFT and parser as the real candidates. mixfeas.py's
* analytic_expectations() holds the closed forms; selftest fails if the
* extraction disagrees. No device model is used.
*
* Ports are sensed, not loaded: the B source senses the RF source's
* open-circuit node rfs (ahead of Rrf, so the LO current injected into
* rf_port below cannot leak into the product) and the unloaded LO legs, so
* the sensed RF voltage is exactly Vrf_open and V(lo_p) - V(lo_n) = vlo.
*   v_rf(t) = vrf1 sin(w1 t) + vrf2 sin(w2 t)      (open circuit, rf_dc = 0)
*   v_lo(t) = vlo sin(wlo t)
* B source e_if, in series with 50 ohm into Rif (= 50 ohm), so
*   V(if_out) = 0.5 * [ ac_k * v_rf * v_lo + ac_k3 * v_rf^3 * v_lo + ac_c * v_lo ]
* LO-to-RF coupling: an ideal VCCS injects ac_g * v_lo into rf_port, whose
* only path to ground is Rrf (50 ohm through the zero RF source), so
*   V(rf_port) at flo = 50 * ac_g * vlo  (when the RF source is off).
* No supply current flows (rail power is exactly 0), and the "devices"
* list for this control is empty.

* ac_k, ac_k3, ac_c, ac_g are .param lines generated from tb.json
* "study.analytic_control.params" (the one place their values live, so the
* closed forms in mixfeas.analytic_expectations use the same numbers).

Bac_if ac_e 0 V = 'ac_k*v(rfs)*(v(lo_p)-v(lo_n)) + ac_k3*v(rfs)*v(rfs)*v(rfs)*(v(lo_p)-v(lo_n)) + ac_c*(v(lo_p)-v(lo_n))'
Rac_s ac_e if_out {z0}
Gac_lo 0 rf_port lo_p lo_n {ac_g}
